that has been with us since we started learning English.

5
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:28,230
Fill in the blanks or Completion.

6
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:31,630
But wait, you think you know it all,

7
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:33,910
but in fact, you don't.

8
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:37,310
This question type in IELTS is very different

9
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:40,530
from the gap-filling exercises we did in the past.

10
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:44,090
Let's find out the differences together.

11
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:49,550
Today's lesson aims to help you understand different

12
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:53,090
formats of completion questions in IELTS Reading.

13
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:57,360
Remember, understand and apply steps

14
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,960
for completion questions effectively.

15
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:03,330
We have three parts of the lesson.

16
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:09,010
1. Definition and formats of completion questions.

