23
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:31,980
Basically, completion questions in IELTS Reading are

24
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:35,830
gap-filling exercises based on the question's requirements.

25
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:41,840
However, there are two big differences between completion questions

26
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,850
and gap-filling exercises that we usually do.

27
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:50,250
Firstly, for completion questions, the answers must be

28
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:51,930
taken from the reading passage.

29
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:55,830
Normally, when we do gap-filling exercises, we

30
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:57,750
have to think about the words we want

31
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:00,510
to write or choose from an available list.

32
00:02:01,030 --> 00:02:03,400
Or, with multiple choice questions,

33
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:06,400
we have four options for each blank.

34
00:02:07,009 --> 00:02:09,130
In IELTS exams, it's different.

35
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:12,030
Let's look at this question.

36
00:02:12,730 --> 00:02:14,650
Choose from the passage.

37
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:18,350
The question clearly says that the answers have

38
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:20,690
to be taken from the reading and you

39
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:22,490
can't write whatever you want.

40
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:25,790
There is only one type of completion that

41
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:27,230
does not follow this rule.

42
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:30,630
We will learn more about it in the next lesson.

43
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:35,530
Because of this specific requirement, you should pay

44
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:40,250
attention to these three DON'Ts when choosing the answer.

45
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:43,770
Don't change the path of speech.

46
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:46,710
Don't change the order.

47
00:02:47,710 --> 00:02:51,330
And, don't change the singular into the plural

48
00:02:51,330 --> 00:02:53,090
and vice versa.

49
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:57,190
Simply speaking, the answers in the blanks must

50
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,630
be exactly the same as those in the

51
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:02,450
reading passage, without any changes.

52
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:06,270
In fact, this requirement helps us check if

53
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:08,990
the answers are correct or not.

54
00:03:09,970 --> 00:03:13,490
For example, the answer needs a singular noun.

55
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:16,630
When scanning in the passage, we found a

56
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:19,590
noun which has a suitable meaning, but it

57
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:21,570
turns out to be a plural noun.

58
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:24,990
It means that this word is not the one we need.

59
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:28,050
There are many students who will still try

60
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:30,350
to remove the plural form of this word

61
00:03:30,350 --> 00:03:33,790
and write it in the blank, but it isn't correct.

62
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:36,410
It's not the answer we need.

63
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:41,100
The second difference compared to the traditional gap-filling exercises

64
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,150
is that in the IELTS reading,

65
00:03:43,150 --> 00:03:46,930
there are seven formats of completion questions.

66
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:51,030
In IELTS reading, instead of filling words into

67
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:53,910
a paragraph, we also have to fill in

68
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:56,990
sentences, tables, or diagrams.

69
00:03:57,550 --> 00:04:00,210
To sum up, I would like to introduce

70
00:04:00,210 --> 00:04:03,570
to you the completion tree, a summary tree

71
00:04:03,570 --> 00:04:05,050
of completion questions.

72
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:12,960
I'm going to divide them into two big groups.

73
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:17,940
The first group is questions with the answers come in order.

74
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:21,300
The second group is the questions

75
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,300
with the answers might not come in order.

76
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:27,880
In the first group, the answer to question 1

77
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:32,300
will appear before the answer to question 2, and so on.

78
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,340
In the second group, most of the answers

79
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:38,960
come in order, but there are some exercises

80
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:41,860
in which the answer to question 2 may

81
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:45,000
appear before the answer to question 1.

82
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:50,580
Questions with the answer come in order are easier,

83
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:53,160
because we can use this order to

84
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,840
locate the information for the questions

85
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,460
that we have not finished.

86
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:00,960
For example, if you have done with questions

87
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:05,440
1 and 3, but not question 2, then

88
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:08,220
the answer to question 2 is only between

89
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,740
the answers of question 1 and 3.

90
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:12,120
Just focus on it.

91
00:05:15,430 --> 00:05:18,590
This completion question type has two formats.

92
00:05:19,790 --> 00:05:23,030
Sentence completion, fill in the blanks to complete

93
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:25,070
the sentence, for example.

94
00:05:26,990 --> 00:05:30,970
And note completion, fill in the blanks to complete the note.

95
00:05:31,530 --> 00:05:34,250
It is the example at the beginning of our lesson.

96
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:39,770
For completion questions in which the answers might

97
00:05:39,770 --> 00:05:41,690
not come in order, we are going to

98
00:05:41,690 --> 00:05:44,350
divide them into three formats based on the

99
00:05:44,350 --> 00:05:45,650
format of the question.

100
00:05:46,370 --> 00:05:50,790
Table or procedure, image and summary.

101
00:05:51,510 --> 00:05:55,910
For table or procedure, we have table completion,

102
00:05:56,650 --> 00:06:00,250
fill in the blanks to complete a given table, for example.

103
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:06,900
And flowchart completion, in which you have to

104
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,140
complete a procedure, like this one.

105
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:16,850
For image, there is only diagram completion.

106
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:22,840
Finally, we have a completion question type in

107
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:25,380
which you have to complete a summary.

108
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,700
This has two formats.

109
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,840
Summary completion with wordlist,

110
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,840
which has given words to fill in.

111
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:36,208
And summary completion without wordlist,

112
00:06:36,208 --> 00:06:38,600
with no given words.

113
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:41,600
We need to understand some differences between these two,

114
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,900
but we'll learn them in another lesson.

115
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,980
For now, you just need to look at

116
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:50,140
the following two examples to have an overview about them.

117
00:06:52,650 --> 00:06:55,520
Actually, many of you may think,

118
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:58,550
why do you give me such a complicated question type

119
00:06:58,550 --> 00:06:59,860
with different formats?

120
00:07:00,530 --> 00:07:03,910
Although there are many formats, the strategy is the same.

121
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:06,930
So don't worry, you can handle them well.

122
00:07:07,410 --> 00:07:09,150
Let's move on to the steps.

123
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:10,370
Let's go.

124
00:07:15,070 --> 00:07:17,240
To handle this question type effectively,

125
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,750
please follow my four steps.

126
00:07:20,850 --> 00:07:25,390
Step number one, read the question's requirement carefully.

127
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:30,910
Step number two, read each question carefully and

128
00:07:30,910 --> 00:07:32,050
predict the answer.

129
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:38,250
Step number three, apply scanning skills to locate information.

130
00:07:39,230 --> 00:07:44,430
And last, step number four, find and fill in the answer.

131
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:46,790
Let's analyze them.

132
00:07:48,030 --> 00:07:52,110
Step one, read the question's requirement carefully.

133
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:56,730
This is a very important step that many candidates skip.

134
00:07:57,570 --> 00:08:00,570
Reading the question's requirements will give us two

135
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:02,790
following pieces of information.

136
00:08:04,010 --> 00:08:06,330
Format of completion question.

137
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:10,290
Number of words required for each answer.

138
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:14,030
For example, let's look at the following questions.

139
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,440
We see that it is table completion.

140
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,080
In the questions, we have complete the table below.

141
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,980
According to the previous part of this lesson,

142
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:33,460
for this format, the answers might not come in order.

143
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:35,620
So pay attention to it.

144
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:38,580
Next, the number of words.

145
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:42,980
No more than two words, which means you

146
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:46,200
just write a maximum of two words.

147
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:49,740
You should underline this phrase because it can

148
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:53,640
affect your score if the answer you write

149
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,940
has the correct information.

150
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,920
But if it exceeds the word limit, then

151
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:02,800
it can still be counted as an incorrect answer.

152
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:07,020
For example, with this word limit, no more

153
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:10,840
than two words, if the answer is two

154
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:14,140
months, but you write a period of two

155
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:17,640
months, then it will not be scored because

156
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:21,420
the word limit is a maximum of two words.

157
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:24,320
Your answer includes five words.

158
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:28,440
If the question's requirement is no more than

159
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:32,360
two words and or a number, we can

160
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:36,440
write a maximum of two words and one number.

161
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:40,060
Step one just needs to be done quickly,

162
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:43,500
but if you don't do it, you will lose points.

163
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:45,960
Let's continue with step two.

164
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:52,980
Step two, read each question carefully and predict the answer.

165
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:56,820
Every time you handle a question, you should

166
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:59,560
read it carefully to use prediction skill.

167
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,780
Predict about the answer you need to write.

168
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:07,380
Prediction skill is very important in completion questions

169
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:10,420
because making detailed predictions will help you find

170
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:13,780
the information faster and more correctly.

171
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:18,020
There are three things you need to predict

172
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,180
for the answer.

173
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:21,460
Part of speech.

174
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:25,160
Does the blank need a noun, a verb,

175
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:28,600
an adjective, or any other parts of speech?

176
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,660
Let's use your grammar to predict it.

177
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:33,780
Content.

178
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:36,720
You already have the part of speech.

179
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,400
Now if you can predict the meaning of

180
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,580
the answer, it will be much easier to

181
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,940
find the correct word or words.

182
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:48,440
For example, is it a noun referring to

183
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:52,020
a person or a noun referring to an

184
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:55,620
object or a noun referring to an event?

185
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:59,100
If it is an adjective, does it have

186
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:01,440
a positive or negative meaning?

187
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:03,140
Grammar.

188
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:08,340
If the answer is a noun, is it a singular or plural noun?

189
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:18,040
If it is a verb, is it to verb, verb with ing, or verb infinitive?

190
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:19,220
Step 3.

191
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:22,560
Apply scanning skills to locate information.

192
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,840
We have learned this skill very carefully at

193
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:28,180
the beginning of the course and also practiced

194
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:32,140
in some lessons, so I think you are familiar with it.

195
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:35,600
I'm going to give you steps for scanning again.

196
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:40,380
Step 1. Identify keywords in the question.

197
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:45,180
Step 2. Identify scanning words among keywords.

198
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:52,080
Step 3. Find keywords, preferably scanning words, or their variations

199
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:54,180
and synonyms in the passage.

200
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,960
Don't forget some extra tips for scanning when

201
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,140
you find their variations and synonyms.

202
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:01,760
Tip number 1.

203
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:06,860
Among scanning words, prefer finding unchangeable keywords,

204
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:07,620
if possible.

205
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:09,380
Tip number 2.

206
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:12,420
Pay attention to other parts of speech of

207
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:15,060
the original keywords in the scanning process.

208
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:17,960
Now it's time for the final step.

209
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:22,480
Step 4. Find and fill in the answer.

210
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:27,420
Based on the predictions in step 2, we

211
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:29,920
will find correct answers and then write them

212
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:33,840
on the answer sheet if you take the paper-based test.

213
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:42,490
Now we have finished 4 steps for completion questions.

214
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:45,210
If we do it step by step, this

215
00:12:45,210 --> 00:12:48,150
question type will no longer be difficult for us.

216
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:51,790
Ok guys, let's take a break before we practice.

